1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:01,814
It's 7 AM.

2
00:00:02,132 --> 00:00:04,268
You open ChatGPT.

3
00:00:04,501 --> 00:00:05,501
Nothing.

4
00:00:05,809 --> 00:00:07,672
You try another AI app.

5
00:00:07,904 --> 00:00:08,904
Nothing.

6
00:00:09,127 --> 00:00:11,102
Your stock app is flashing red.

7
00:00:11,462 --> 00:00:13,461
And it all happened because one company,

8
00:00:13,501 --> 00:00:16,658
worth about three trillion
dollars, disappeared overnight.

9
00:00:17,273 --> 00:00:19,181
This is a thought experiment.

10
00:00:19,354 --> 00:00:21,489
But every number you'll hear is real.

11
00:00:21,849 --> 00:00:25,120
So... what actually happens
if NVIDIA vanished tomorrow?

12
00:00:25,905 --> 00:00:28,093
First, what does NVIDIA even do?

13
00:00:28,453 --> 00:00:30,724
It makes chips called GPUs.

14
00:00:30,897 --> 00:00:34,321
Think of a normal computer
chip as one very smart chef.

15
00:00:34,494 --> 00:00:38,861
A GPU is a kitchen with thousands of
cooks, all chopping at the same time.

16
00:00:39,034 --> 00:00:40,861
And that's exactly what AI needs:

17
00:00:40,901 --> 00:00:44,050
billions of tiny maths
problems, solved all at once.

18
00:00:44,410 --> 00:00:46,993
So GPUs are the engines of AI.

19
00:00:47,166 --> 00:00:49,239
And NVIDIA makes most of them.

20
00:00:49,412 --> 00:00:54,363
By most estimates, about 80 percent of
the AI chips in the world's data centers.

21
00:00:54,723 --> 00:00:56,884
But chips are only half the story.

22
00:00:57,057 --> 00:00:59,159
The other half is called CUDA.

23
00:00:59,332 --> 00:01:03,052
CUDA is the language programmers
use to talk to NVIDIA chips.

24
00:01:03,225 --> 00:01:07,111
NVIDIA says more than 11 million
developers build with it.

25
00:01:07,284 --> 00:01:10,387
That's twenty years of
code, tools... and habits.

26
00:01:10,747 --> 00:01:12,220
Remember that word.

27
00:01:12,325 --> 00:01:13,325
Habits.

28
00:01:13,387 --> 00:01:14,668
It matters later.

29
00:01:15,028 --> 00:01:20,609
In just the last three months, NVIDIA
made 115.8 billion dollars in sales.

30
00:01:20,782 --> 00:01:24,052
And 107.6 billion of that
came from data centers:

31
00:01:24,092 --> 00:01:26,673
the giant buildings where AI lives.

32
00:01:27,458 --> 00:01:28,941
So let's play it out.

33
00:01:29,301 --> 00:01:30,301
Midnight.

34
00:01:30,498 --> 00:01:32,722
In our story, NVIDIA is gone.

35
00:01:32,895 --> 00:01:35,892
And every NVIDIA chip on
Earth goes dark with it.

36
00:01:36,507 --> 00:01:37,672
Hour one.

37
00:01:37,862 --> 00:01:39,888
The data centers go quiet.

38
00:01:40,248 --> 00:01:44,689
ChatGPT, used by nearly a billion
people every week, can't answer.

39
00:01:44,862 --> 00:01:46,606
Image makers freeze.

40
00:01:46,711 --> 00:01:48,783
Voice assistants go silent.

41
00:01:48,888 --> 00:01:51,459
Coding tools stop halfway through a line.

42
00:01:51,819 --> 00:01:53,640
A few services survive.

43
00:01:53,813 --> 00:01:58,013
Google, for example, runs a lot of
its AI on its own chips, called TPUs.

44
00:01:58,186 --> 00:02:01,172
But most of the AI world
was built on NVIDIA.

45
00:02:01,345 --> 00:02:03,442
So most of it simply stops.

46
00:02:03,802 --> 00:02:05,631
And it's not just chatbots.

47
00:02:05,804 --> 00:02:08,456
Hospitals using AI to read scans.

48
00:02:08,561 --> 00:02:10,894
Banks using AI to catch fraud.

49
00:02:10,999 --> 00:02:12,357
Weather forecasts.

50
00:02:12,462 --> 00:02:14,658
Scientists testing new medicines.

51
00:02:14,831 --> 00:02:16,456
All of it slows down.

52
00:02:16,604 --> 00:02:17,642
Or stops.

53
00:02:18,427 --> 00:02:19,427
Day one.

54
00:02:19,607 --> 00:02:21,443
The stock market opens.

55
00:02:21,616 --> 00:02:23,672
And this is where it gets scary.

56
00:02:24,032 --> 00:02:30,494
NVIDIA alone is about 5 percent of the
S&P 500: America's 500 biggest companies.

57
00:02:30,667 --> 00:02:32,204
So if you own a simple index fund,

58
00:02:32,244 --> 00:02:35,454
part of your money was in NVIDIA,
maybe without you even knowing.

59
00:02:35,814 --> 00:02:37,929
That slice just went to zero.

60
00:02:38,289 --> 00:02:40,454
About three trillion dollars.

61
00:02:40,686 --> 00:02:42,266
Gone in one morning.

62
00:02:42,626 --> 00:02:46,425
That's about three-quarters of
India's entire yearly economy.

63
00:02:46,598 --> 00:02:49,320
Hold on to that thought.
We'll come back to India.

64
00:02:49,680 --> 00:02:51,311
And it doesn't stop there.

65
00:02:51,484 --> 00:02:53,899
Companies that make parts for NVIDIA.

66
00:02:54,004 --> 00:02:56,458
Companies that rent out NVIDIA chips.

67
00:02:56,563 --> 00:02:58,902
Companies whose whole plan was AI.

68
00:02:59,075 --> 00:03:02,922
They all fall together, because suddenly,
nobody knows what anything is worth.

69
00:03:03,282 --> 00:03:05,700
Want a real-world hint of how that feels?

70
00:03:05,873 --> 00:03:11,439
In early October 2026, NVIDIA was
worth about 5.8 trillion dollars.

71
00:03:11,612 --> 00:03:16,682
In just over six weeks, about 2.7 trillion
dollars of that value disappeared.

72
00:03:16,855 --> 00:03:18,754
Markets everywhere felt it.

73
00:03:18,927 --> 00:03:22,364
Now imagine not a fall... but
the whole thing, gone at once.

74
00:03:23,149 --> 00:03:24,189
Week one.

75
00:03:24,379 --> 00:03:26,160
The tech giants panic.

76
00:03:26,520 --> 00:03:27,491
Before all this,

77
00:03:27,531 --> 00:03:30,238
NVIDIA said it could
see around 500 billion

78
00:03:30,278 --> 00:03:33,367
dollars of chip orders
lined up through 2026.

79
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:37,711
Microsoft, Amazon, Meta, OpenAI: they
were all waiting for those chips.

80
00:03:37,884 --> 00:03:40,431
Now those orders point to... nothing.

81
00:03:40,791 --> 00:03:42,181
So who steps in?

82
00:03:42,354 --> 00:03:47,049
AMD makes AI chips too, and OpenAI
had already signed a deal to use them.

83
00:03:47,222 --> 00:03:49,278
Google has its TPUs.

84
00:03:49,383 --> 00:03:51,970
Amazon has its own chips, called Trainium.

85
00:03:52,143 --> 00:03:53,985
So why not just switch?

86
00:03:54,345 --> 00:03:55,618
Three reasons.

87
00:03:55,978 --> 00:03:57,488
One: factories.

88
00:03:57,636 --> 00:03:59,221
Advanced chips take years to plan,

89
00:03:59,261 --> 00:04:02,231
and the factories that make
them are already booked solid.

90
00:04:02,591 --> 00:04:03,958
Two: CUDA.

91
00:04:04,106 --> 00:04:05,639
Remember those habits?

92
00:04:05,812 --> 00:04:08,936
Millions of programs are
written in NVIDIA's language.

93
00:04:09,109 --> 00:04:13,008
Moving them is like translating a
giant library... one book at a time.

94
00:04:13,368 --> 00:04:15,209
Three: the full package.

95
00:04:15,357 --> 00:04:17,579
NVIDIA doesn't just sell chips.

96
00:04:17,684 --> 00:04:21,231
It sells the cables, the networking,
the software... the whole machine.

97
00:04:21,404 --> 00:04:23,641
Rivals have pieces of the puzzle.

98
00:04:23,746 --> 00:04:26,115
Nobody has the whole puzzle ready.

99
00:04:26,475 --> 00:04:29,830
So the price of every AI chip
still available shoots up.

100
00:04:30,003 --> 00:04:32,504
Renting AI power becomes a luxury.

101
00:04:33,289 --> 00:04:35,378
Now, what happens to India?

102
00:04:35,738 --> 00:04:38,288
India isn't watching this from far away.

103
00:04:38,461 --> 00:04:40,929
India is deeply wired into NVIDIA.

104
00:04:41,289 --> 00:04:43,691
NVIDIA has thousands
of engineers in India,

105
00:04:43,731 --> 00:04:46,380
in Bengaluru, Hyderabad,
Pune and Gurugram.

106
00:04:46,553 --> 00:04:50,002
They design chips and write
software that the whole world uses.

107
00:04:50,175 --> 00:04:53,611
In our story, those teams
wake up... with no company.

108
00:04:54,226 --> 00:04:56,434
Then there's the IndiaAI Mission.

109
00:04:56,607 --> 00:04:58,925
The government has made more than 38,000

110
00:04:58,965 --> 00:05:01,932
GPUs available to Indian
startups and researchers,

111
00:05:01,972 --> 00:05:04,185
and most of them are NVIDIA chips.

112
00:05:04,358 --> 00:05:09,997
For example, Sarvam AI trained its
biggest model on 4,096 NVIDIA chips.

113
00:05:10,170 --> 00:05:13,589
Overnight, India's own AI
dream loses its engine.

114
00:05:13,949 --> 00:05:16,619
India's big new AI data centers?

115
00:05:16,792 --> 00:05:19,116
From Reliance in Jamnagar
to Yotta's planned

116
00:05:19,156 --> 00:05:21,372
cluster of more than 20,000 NVIDIA chips,

117
00:05:21,412 --> 00:05:23,227
they were built around NVIDIA.

118
00:05:23,400 --> 00:05:26,104
Billions of dollars of
plans, suddenly stuck.

119
00:05:26,464 --> 00:05:32,218
Indian IT is a 315 billion dollar
industry, with nearly 6 million workers.

120
00:05:32,391 --> 00:05:33,248
Infosys, TCS,

121
00:05:33,288 --> 00:05:38,409
Wipro and HCLTech all build AI services
for clients using NVIDIA tools.

122
00:05:38,582 --> 00:05:40,305
Those projects freeze.

123
00:05:40,410 --> 00:05:42,209
Clients pause spending.

124
00:05:42,314 --> 00:05:44,846
And when clients pause, hiring slows.

125
00:05:45,206 --> 00:05:46,580
What about gamers?

126
00:05:46,728 --> 00:05:48,240
Here's a surprise.

127
00:05:48,413 --> 00:05:51,896
Most of India's 555 million
gamers play on phones,

128
00:05:51,936 --> 00:05:55,046
and phones mostly don't use NVIDIA chips.

129
00:05:55,219 --> 00:05:57,343
So mobile gaming survives!

130
00:05:57,516 --> 00:05:59,585
But PC gamers get a shock.

131
00:05:59,690 --> 00:06:02,742
Graphics cards become
rare, and very expensive.

132
00:06:03,102 --> 00:06:04,467
And the stock market?

133
00:06:04,640 --> 00:06:05,734
When Wall Street panics,

134
00:06:05,774 --> 00:06:09,610
foreign investors often pull money out
of markets like India to play it safe.

135
00:06:09,783 --> 00:06:13,558
That could drag down the Sensex and the
Nifty, and put pressure on the rupee.

136
00:06:13,731 --> 00:06:17,227
Even Indian companies with no
link to NVIDIA could feel it.

137
00:06:17,587 --> 00:06:19,256
But here's the other side.

138
00:06:19,429 --> 00:06:22,583
If the whole world has to rewrite
its AI software for new chips...

139
00:06:22,623 --> 00:06:24,999
who has millions of
engineers ready to do it?

140
00:06:25,359 --> 00:06:26,594
India does.

141
00:06:27,379 --> 00:06:28,552
Month six.

142
00:06:28,742 --> 00:06:30,686
The world starts to rebuild.

143
00:06:31,046 --> 00:06:34,144
AMD and Google make chips
as fast as they can.

144
00:06:34,317 --> 00:06:36,863
Governments pour money into new factories.

145
00:06:37,036 --> 00:06:40,832
Programmers move old CUDA code
to new platforms, line by line.

146
00:06:41,005 --> 00:06:44,075
And NVIDIA's former engineers,
some of the best in the world,

147
00:06:44,115 --> 00:06:46,203
get hired by rivals almost instantly.

148
00:06:46,376 --> 00:06:48,382
Because the knowledge didn't vanish.

149
00:06:48,487 --> 00:06:49,742
It just moved.

150
00:06:50,102 --> 00:06:51,668
AI comes back.

151
00:06:51,773 --> 00:06:53,861
But slower, and more expensive.

152
00:06:54,034 --> 00:06:56,558
For a while, the future is put on pause.

153
00:06:57,173 --> 00:06:58,312
Year one.

154
00:06:58,502 --> 00:07:00,022
The map looks different.

155
00:07:00,195 --> 00:07:03,744
Instead of one giant, there are
five or six serious chipmakers.

156
00:07:03,917 --> 00:07:05,406
More competition.

157
00:07:05,511 --> 00:07:06,845
A slower start.

158
00:07:06,950 --> 00:07:10,555
But a stronger system, one that can't
be knocked out by a single blow.

159
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,820
So what's the lesson?

160
00:07:13,180 --> 00:07:15,170
When the whole world leans on one company,

161
00:07:15,210 --> 00:07:17,680
that company becomes a
single point of failure.

162
00:07:17,853 --> 00:07:20,152
It's like a city with only one bridge.

163
00:07:20,325 --> 00:07:23,270
Everything works perfectly...
until it doesn't.

164
00:07:23,885 --> 00:07:25,432
And here's the twist.

165
00:07:25,792 --> 00:07:28,291
NVIDIA doesn't even make its own chips.

166
00:07:28,464 --> 00:07:32,272
It designs them, but they're
manufactured by another company: TSMC.

167
00:07:32,445 --> 00:07:36,181
So even the company the world depends
on... depends on someone else.

168
00:07:36,796 --> 00:07:38,214
Which makes you wonder:

169
00:07:38,319 --> 00:07:41,000
which company does the
world depend on next?

170
00:07:41,360 --> 00:07:42,993
Tell me in the comments.

171
00:07:43,353 --> 00:07:46,534
And if you enjoyed this, subscribe
for more 'What If' stories.
